== About me
I am a Ph.D. candidate at [https://www.imperial.ac.uk/business-school/ Imperial Business School] under the advice of [https://xiaocheng-li.github.io/ Prof. Xiaocheng Li] and [https://profiles.imperial.ac.uk/kalyan.talluri/ Prof. Kalyan Talluri].\n
Previously, I visited the [https://msande.stanford.edu/ Department of Management Science and Engineering] at Stanford University, hosted by [https://web.stanford.edu/~jblanche/ Prof. Jose Blanchet].\n
I received my M.Res. degree from Imperial College Business School in 2022.
Before joining Imperial College, I received my B.Sc. degree from [https://www.math.pku.edu.cn/ School of Mathematical Sciences] at Peking University in 2021.\n
For those who are interested, my Chinese name is 刘(Liu)上(Shang).\n
*I am on the academic job market of 2026.*\n
Here is my [CV.pdf CV].

== Research
My current research interests include:
- Machine Learning, Large Language Models, and Operations Research

Within these broad areas, I am interested in theoretically grounded methodological research and in theory that offers useful insights into why methods work, when they work, and where their limitations lie. My interests are not limited to the topics I have worked on so far, and I am always open to discussing new problems and potential collaborations.

